   "residual": -1,
   "committed": false,
   "why": "The 21 lines read come to 34 against a footing of 33. One person out is not a reading dispute that can be split - it is one cell somewhere in the column - and on this exposure there are three cells that could carry it: line 2 (read 6, alternate 5), line 7 (read 2, alternate 1) and line 16 (read 4, alternate 1). The project's rule is that a column commits only when the lines READ sum to the footing, so this column is NOT committed. Its reading is kept whole in cells_first_pass, where nothing downstream can consume it as fact and the next reader starts from a reading rather than from the sheet."
