 "cells_state": "read_partly_reconciled",
 "what_the_sheet_says": "Twenty-one households, 100 people, and an agriculture column with an entry against nearly every line of them. Not one person on the leaf is returned in commerce, in manufactures and trades, in navigation or in the learned professions, and the enumerator footed no column but those two. Whatever district this leaf belongs to, it is farmed and not traded, which is the opposite of the town: printed page 219's continuation (33S7-9YYJ-24) foots agriculture 2 and commerce 9 and manufactures 27 over 201 people. It is LATER EVIDENCE under this domain's rule and it names nobody - the names are on a left sheet nobody has found.",
 "an_unread_mark": "One mark stands alone on the leaf outside the two written columns: a small V-shaped tick at about x=3610, y=800, inside the SCHOOLS, &c. block, at roughly the height of line 2. It is not a numeral and the column it sits in carries no footing, so it is recorded as seen and read as nothing. Every other cell of every other column is blank on all 21 lines.",
